  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Find separator color and separator rows/cols:\n    # rows/cols entirely filled with the same non-zero color.\n    sep_color = None\n    sep_rows = []\n    sep_cols = []\n\n    for r in range(h):\n        vals = set(grid[r])\n        if len(vals) == 1:\n            v = next(iter(vals))\n            if v != 0:\n                sep_rows.append(r)\n                sep_color = v\n\n    for c in range(w):\n        vals = {grid[r][c] for r in range(h)}\n        if len(vals) == 1:\n            v = next(iter(vals))\n            if v != 0:\n                sep_cols.append(c)\n                if sep_color is None:\n                    sep_color = v\n\n    # Determine the non-separator non-zero object color.\n    colors = set()\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v != 0 and v != sep_color:\n                colors.add(v)\n    obj_color = next(iter(colors)) if colors else None\n\n    # Build row and column blocks between separator lines.\n    row_bounds = [-1] + sep_rows + [h]\n    col_bounds = [-1] + sep_cols + [w]\n\n    row_blocks = []\n    for i in range(len(row_bounds) - 1):\n        a, b = row_bounds[i] + 1, row_bounds[i + 1]\n        if a < b:\n            row_blocks.append((a, b))\n\n    col_blocks = []\n    for i in range(len(col_bounds) - 1):\n        a, b = col_bounds[i] + 1, col_bounds[i + 1]\n        if a < b:\n            col_blocks.append((a, b))\n\n    # Find template: the subgrid with the largest number of object-color cells.\n    template = set()\n    template_h = template_w = None\n\n    for rs, re in row_blocks:\n        for cs, ce in col_blocks:\n            positions = set()\n            for r in range(rs, re):\n                for c in range(cs, ce):\n                    if grid[r][c] == obj_color:\n                        positions.add((r - rs, c - cs))\n            if len(positions) > len(template):\n                template = positions\n                template_h = re - rs\n                template_w = ce - cs\n\n    # Apply template to every subgrid:\n    # fill missing template cells with separator color, preserving object cells.\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    for rs, re in row_blocks:\n        for cs, ce in col_blocks:\n            if (re - rs) != template_h or (ce - cs) != template_w:\n                continue\n            for dr, dc in template:\n                r, c = rs + dr, cs + dc\n                if out[r][c] == 0:\n                    out[r][c] = sep_color\n\n    return out",
